{# NX·01 · THE HONEST FUTURE-MODULE SLOT.

   IT INVENTS NOTHING, because there is nothing to invent: a module that is not installed in this
   area has contributed no widget, no tile, no item and no layer, and a card that drew its figures
   would be a fake module rather than an honest affordance. What it names is what the catalogue
   holds and the rule that installing one adds a headed section to the library — and nothing else
   on this page changes, and no preset is invalidated, because a preset that never named the new
   widgets simply does not show them. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">NX·01</span>Not installed in this area<span class="src">· {{ by.next.catalogueCount }} in the catalogue · {{ by.next.absent|length }} not here</span></span>
    {{ include('area/overview/_ao_by.html.twig', {slug: 'next', who: 'the seam'}, with_context: false) }}

    {% if by.next.absent is empty %}
        <div class="use">Every module the catalogue holds is switched on in this area. When a new one is added to the
            catalogue it appears here first, before anybody installs it.</div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="use" style="margin:0 2px 12px">Nothing below is drawn with invented data, because there is none. Only
            an installed module’s provider can say what it would put on this page, and these have not been asked.</div>
        <div class="ao-slot">
            {% for module in by.next.absent %}
                <div class="ao-slotrow">
                    <span class="nm">{{ module.name }}</span>
                    <span class="wd">{{ module.source|default('No description in the catalogue.') }}</span>
                    <span class="st">in the catalogue</span>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="rln" style="margin-top:12px">
        <span class="fog">What installing one changes on this page</span>
        <span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">a headed section in the library · nothing else</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">What it changes in the host</span>
        <span class="mono acc" style="font-size:11px">nothing — new tagged provider classes only</span>
    </div>
    <a class="open-btn" href="{{ urls.customize }}" style="margin-top:10px">Add a module to this area →</a>
</div>
